  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="commodity_jacket_cb5a06c99dc0a46c6fc75b6e1b7a842398edbd03b55718f62d30e3449050121648">
    <crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>Short coats for the upper body made in various forms and lengths, but usually no lower than the waist or upper hip; worn indoors or for light warmth and protection from the weather. [Source: Getty AAT] | a short and close-fitting upper garment of men and women; a jacket; especially coat of fence, a kind of sleeveless tunic or jacket, formerly worn by foot-soldiers and others, usually of leather quilted, and in later times often plated with iron (OED s.v. jack n.2 1a-1b)</crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>
    <crm:P2_has_type rdf:resource="http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object"/>
  </rdf:Description>
